  "meta": {
    "title": "The Darién Gap: The Road That Stops in the Jungle 🌴🇵🇦🇨🇴😱",
    "description": "The Pan-American Highway runs about 30,000 km from Alaska 🇺🇸 to the tip of Argentina 🇦🇷 but it has one gap 🛑 Between Yaviza in Panama 🇵🇦 and Turbo in Colombia 🇨🇴 there's no road for about 106 km: the Darién Gap 🌴 A road was planned in 1971 and halted in 1974, and swamps, mountains, rainforest, deadly wildlife 🐍 and violent crime make it one of the most dangerous places on Earth. Still, in 2023 more than 520,000 people crossed it on foot 😱",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "30,000 km of highway… and 106 km of jungle 🌴😱",
      "Would you ever try to cross the Darién Gap? 👇",
      "Which dangerous place should we cover next? 🗺️"
    ],
